// aug04d2 fuzz/000000 (2026-08-05): NONDETERMINISTIC COMPILE
// ACCEPTANCE — ~20% of fresh processes rejected this program
// ("str::parse requires a concrete return type"), ~80% accepted and
// ran it. The unconstrained parse return settled as Array<⊥> under
// one per-process unification order (accepted by extract_cast_type's
// Set-only ⊥ walk) and stayed open under another (rejected). Eric's
// ruling: COMPILE-REJECT, no question — ⊥ anywhere in a cast target
// is a settle artifact (the jul14b family, nested in a composite
// constructor where the ⊥-member net didn't reach). Fixed: the
// contains_bottom walk descends Array/Tuple/Struct/Variant/Map/Error/
// ByRef. Both modes now reject deterministically (CompileErr-agree).
// The SEED nondeterminism (async module-load order shifting all
// id/tvar minting) and the settle order-sensitivity remain latent —
// tracked in fuzz/pending-triage/parse_concrete_settle_flap.gx.
array::window(#n: i64:1, str::parse("notanumber")?, never())
